NNAAMMEE
     ssyyssuuppggrraaddee — upgrade system to the next release or a new snapshot

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ssyyssuuppggrraaddee [--ffkknnss] [--bb _b_a_s_e_-_d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y] [--RR _v_e_r_s_i_o_n] [_i_n_s_t_a_l_l_u_r_l | _p_a_t_h]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     ssyyssuuppggrraaddee is a utility to upgrade OpenBSD to a new release or snapshot
     if available.

     ssyyssuuppggrraaddee downloads the necessary files to _/_h_o_m_e_/___s_y_s_u_p_g_r_a_d_e, verifies
     them with signify(1), and copies bsd.rd to _/_b_s_d_._u_p_g_r_a_d_e.

     ssyyssuuppggrraaddee by default then reboots the system.  The bootloader will auto‐
     matically choose _/_b_s_d_._u_p_g_r_a_d_e, triggering a one-shot upgrade using the
     files in _/_h_o_m_e_/___s_y_s_u_p_g_r_a_d_e.

     The options are as follows:

     --bb _b_a_s_e_-_d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y
             Download files to _b_a_s_e_-_d_i_r_e_c_t_o_r_y/___s_y_s_u_p_g_r_a_d_e instead of
             _/_h_o_m_e_/___s_y_s_u_p_g_r_a_d_e.

     --ff      For snapshots, force an already applied upgrade.  This option has
             no effect on releases.

     --kk      Keep the files in _/_h_o_m_e_/___s_y_s_u_p_g_r_a_d_e.  By default they will be
             deleted after the upgrade.

     --nn      Fetch and verify the files and create _/_b_s_d_._u_p_g_r_a_d_e but do not re‐
             boot.

     --RR _v_e_r_s_i_o_n
             Upgrade to a specific release version.  Only upgrades from one
             version to the next are tested.  Skipping versions may work.
             Downgrading is unlikely to work.

     --ss      Upgrade to a snapshot.  The default is to upgrade to the next re‐
             lease.

     When updating to a release or snapshot which lacks the required signify
     keys in _/_e_t_c_/_s_i_g_n_i_f_y, the missing keys will be downloaded in a secure
     way.  In the usual case, the keys will already be present because OpenBSD
     releases ship with the current key, the next key, and a collection of
     older keys.

     See upgrade.site(5) for how to customize the upgrade process.

FFIILLEESS
     /auto_upgrade.conf  Response file for the ramdisk kernel.
     /bsd.upgrade        The ramdisk kernel to trigger an unattended upgrade.
     /etc/installurl     OpenBSD mirror top-level URL for fetching an upgrade.
     /home/_sysupgrade   Directory the upgrade is downloaded to.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     signify(1), installurl(5), upgrade.site(5), autoinstall(8), release(8),
     sysmerge(8)

